WEBVTT

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.060
Daddy, you get in too.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.010
Daddy!

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.010
It's okay.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.680
Luna...

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.080
However painful things may be...

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.550
...or however tough, don't give up.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.380
Live... until the end.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.100
Live...

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.800
...Luna... Daddy!

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.080
Daddy!

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.040
DADDY!!

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:28.990
DADDY!!!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.670
I'm the transfer student, Luna!

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.990
I had that same dream again.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:32.890
Good morning, Dad, Mom.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.130
Oh no! It's already this late?

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:50.890
Chako! It's my first day after transferring!
Why didn't you wake me up?

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.060
What're you talkin' about?
Luna, you're already fourteen, ain't'cha?

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.800
You gotta learn to take care of yourself.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.840
Aw, yeesh! I'm gonna be late!

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.540
Not goin' with that case
of bed-head, are you?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.660
See you later!

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.910
Your breakfast's ready.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.700
I don't need it. Lock up behind
me, okay? Have a nice day.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.580
I guess it's hard to be a
self-supporting student.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:34.800
How's this?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.090
Finished rechargin' my Hydrogen.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.130
This is space colony Roca A-2.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.000
In the 21st century, mankind successfully implemented Anti-gravity and Warp navigation...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.650
...and embarked on full-blown
space development.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:26.360
In the hundred years since then,
wonderful growth was achieved.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:34.690
In the 22nd century, people live in colonies, and more than 30 artificial planets were built in space.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:51.390
Unaware of the blessings entrusted to them,
as always, people choose the easy way.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.400
And yet, I'm running.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:04.950
This is bad news. I shouldn't be late all of a sudden. Maybe I should just take an Air Taxi.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.940
Balance: $15. Balance: $15

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:14.030
Things are tight again this month.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.690
Fine, I'll make it if I run!

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:33.300
Riding a bike on the sidewalk...
Only some rich folks do stuff
like buy vehicles.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.430
Wait a sec! Aren't I in the upper class too?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.850
Make way, make way!

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.640
That's dangerous! Yeesh!

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.030
If you don't run, you'll be late.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.940
I made it...

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.730
I haven't seen your face before.
Are you a transfer student?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.480
Y- yes!

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:46.460
I'll overlook it this time, but it's forbidden to run on the pavement at my prestigious Soria Academy.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.990
Next time I catch you,
I'll impose the punishment.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.380
I hope you'll be more careful.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.290
Y- Yeah.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.780
You should reply, "Yes." Y- yes!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:12.230
Who is that person?

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.440
Menori, the Student Body President.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.640
Why is the student body
president doing the gate check?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.190
She also serves as the
head of the neighbourhood.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.490
This school looks cheerful, but it's strict.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.580
As to be expected of a prestigious school.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.530
Um... who are you?

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.530
Ah, I'm Luna. Nice to meet you!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.010
I'm Sharla. Nice to meet you too.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.640
Luna, where did you come here from?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:43.650
Mars.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:52.430
I saw on TV that beasts live in the undeveloped areas of Mars and Pluto, but is it really true?

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.150
Of course not!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.650
Do it over!

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:00.260
Do you think my eyes are knotholes?

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.580
There's still a little dirt on the sole.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.650
I'm sorry.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:15.410
Howard. It'd be best if you
didn't have anything to do with him.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:20.360
He's the son of a man of influence in this colony, and uses that to do whatever he wants.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.990
Do mine over too!

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.150
Mine too!

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.180
Shine them up nice!

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.900
It bothers me that people who grew up
on Pluto do such a half-hearted job.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:31.910
It's true!

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.140
You guys should at least wash your own shoes.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.860
What did you say?

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.400
Stay out of it!

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:50.960
And Pluto is a fine planet
abundant in natural resources.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.600
There's no reason to be ashamed
of growing up on Pluto.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.480
You don't seem to know, so I'll fill you in.

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:06.080
This guy's old man was picked up
by my Papa and works at Papa's company.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.610
And what of it?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:08.890
Listen up!

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:12.340
This guy was the one who
said he wanted to wash our shoes!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.280
Isn't that right, Bell?

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.150
Is that how you really feel?

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:28.730
Have them cleaned by today's Gym class.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.780
You're your own person!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:49.620
Er, Luna here grew up on a Mars colony, won the scholarship generously donated to this school to

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.130
by the Howard Group, and moved here.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:04.880
In our class, on top of Shingo who skipped
two grades for excellent performance...

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:11.290
...she is our second new addition.
Everyone, please get along with her.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.180
I'm Luna. It's nice to meet all of you.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.940
Take that open seat there.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:20.180
Okay.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.210
I'm glad I'm next to you, Sharla!

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.130
I'm glad too.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:30.450
So, I'll explain about the school trip
which is finally coming up next week.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:37.840
Now, the chief objective of this trip to get personal experience of how planetary settling is done,

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.750
as part of your social studies.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:43.910
Computer, light off, hologram on.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:49.240
This is Earth circa the
beginning of the 21st century.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:54.300
Depletion of the Ozone Layer, air pollution, and Greenhouse effect added up to abnormal weather...

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:58.690
...and around the middle of the 21st century, a large-scale change in the earth's crust occurred...

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:03.980
...and Earth underwent a destructive change
which made it uninhabitable for humans.

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:10.500
Mankind flew away from that disaster,
and embarked on space development.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.740
The first place mankind settled was Mars.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:21.450
After a hundred years, Mankind established
a colony on Mars where humans could live.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:27.340
Under those harsh circumstances,
many pioneers lost their lives.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.830
Planetary training--I can hardly wait!

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.840
Really? I'd rather go to an amusement park.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:45.560
But we can get personal
experience in planetary settlement.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:48.830
Doesn't that seem like fun? I'm not sure.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:53.700
My dream is to be a planetary
settlement technician.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:01.610
That's strange. This locker
was available until recently.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:07.350
Hey, Luna doesn't have a
locker. Is there one free?

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.110
I don't know.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.650
Why don't you look for yourself?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:17.700
Sharla, we've been thinking that you're a transfer student too, and your locker might disappear!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.700
Hey, what do you mean by that?

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.090
Howard...

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:30.680
Because of this morning's incident,
he's trying to make us feel left out.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.240
It'd be fine it's that's all it was.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.650
Why can't we just get along? Right?

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:40.650
Sharla?

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:45.860
What should we do? Starting today,
we're going to be ignored by everyone.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:50.440
I said it's fine! I'm still with you. Okay?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:18.790
Okay! Everyone not in the
game, practice passing.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:24.110
Then, A and B teams, get on the first court.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.660
Menori, take care of that game.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.640
Yes.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:38.440
Both teams, I want a fair and square match.
Switch on your anti-gravity.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:48.900
Then, we'll start the game of Air Basketball.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.410
That's dirty!

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:02.060
Committing fouls when the referee
isn't looking is a skill!

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.290
That's foul play! It was unavoidable.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.250
Foul!

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.430
Are you okay?

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.160
This is why I don't like
people with slow reflexes.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:37.390
What a relief. Your glasses didn't break.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:40.200
Thank you. Sorry, Luna.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.280
Maybe I should just sit out.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.680
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:50.250
I mean, if I stay in,
something worse might happen.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:54.710
I know they did it on purpose.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:58.390
So I don't want to give up here.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:06.410
If you sit out now, they get what they
wanted. I definitely don't want to lose.

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:08.550
Luna...

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:11.740
Can you continue?

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:15.710
Yes.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.620
Sharla!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.660
Bell, watch out!

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:25.240
Continue the game!

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.280
Sharla, go for it!

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:36.830
Luna!

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.650
Like I'd let you!

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:02.440
Goal!

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:08.400
Sharla! We did it!

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.290
Luna, that was amazing!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:13.880
Are you okay?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:16.650
Kaoru! You did that on purpose!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.010
It's fine if the ref doesn't see, right?

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.140
I'll remember this...

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.560
All right!

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:45.490
So Luna, you're living alone?

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.440
What about your parents?

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:50.930
My dad died in an accident when I was eight.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:54.040
Two years before that,
my mom got space sickness and died.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.640
Sorry... I asked something strange.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:03.010
No, it's okay! They both live on
inside my heart, so I'm never lonely!

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:12.600
That's impressive. If I was told I had
to live on my own, I'd never make it.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:15.560
It's nothing serious once you get used to it.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.580
Come to think if it, I'm not really alone.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.780
Chako, my ditzy Robot Pet is with me too.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:30.410
Is somebody spreadin' rumours about me?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.050
The girl who owns me is mean!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.990
A ditzy Robot Pet is pretty rare.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:42.980
Isn't it? And I'm going
through money troubles.

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.980
Make way, make way!

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:52.990
That kid again!

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.240
Look out!

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.310
Are you okay? Yeah, somehow.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.160
Oh. In that case, I guess it's okay.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.310
It's a pretty interesting vehicle.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:16.130
Ah, this? It's my creation.
And it uses gasoline.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:21.110
Huh? Fossil fuel?
That's supposed to be banned in the colony.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.510
And there's the problem of the exhaust.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:27.150
I'd rather you didn't interrupt our
conversation with your personal opinions.

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:30.900
What I make alone won't
have much of an effect.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:35.140
But the thing is... What?
Let's see you repeat that!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.640
I said you guys are worthless.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.700
Damn you!

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:48.790
You think you can go against
us in our own school?

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:56.250
If Howard's pop feels like it, he can make it so you can't live in this colony, let alone go to school.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:59.740
Worthless. You make me want to puke.

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:00.530
Go!

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:01.750
You...

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.280
I don't have the time to
bother with scum like you.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.210
Shove off!

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:11.210
Take him on all at once!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.080
Stop that! You shouldn't fight!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:20.810
You're in the way. Move it! I won't move! And it's cowardly to have so many against one.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:26.700
Shut up. Unless you don't care if I tell
Papa to take away your scholarship money.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:31.200
If you want to do it, then go ahead.
I won't be deterred by something like that!

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.060
This...

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.460
Sharla! Run for it!

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.360
This has nothing to do with me!

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.370
Sharla!

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.410
Sharla! Climb all the way up to the top!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:10.990
Faster!

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:27.790
Live, Luna.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.100
Daddy!

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:32.180
Live!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.950
Sharla?

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.400
Open! Open!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:48.680
Sharla...

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.610
What should we do?
You call the fire department.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:54.830
That's dangerous! It's impossible!

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:13.500
Open! Open!

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:14.960
Sharla!

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:15.860
Luna...

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:19.380
Luna! Move out of the way.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:45.710
Luna...

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.480
Shar... la...

00:23:01.390 --> 00:23:05.180
Brightly burning flames,
surging hot air, creaking stairs.

00:23:05.180 --> 00:23:06.710
I've done all I can.

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:10.010
It was a short life, but thanks, Chako.

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:11.360
Goodbye.

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.540
Doofus! If you don't give it your all here, what'll happen? At this rate, Sharla'll die too!

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:18.980
Did'ja forget what your dad said already?

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:20.100
Live!

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:25.130
Yeah, that! I haven't forgotten at
all! Alright, my energy is back!

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:29.510
Next episode: Impossible to
Avoid!? I won't give up!
